course: dictionary
lesson: 72
title: The acre: a measure of land
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An acre is a unit for measuring how big a piece of land is, like a field, a farm or a garden. Just as a metre measures length, an acre measures area. «A big farm field can be many acres.» So when you read acres, think about the size of the land, not its length or its height.
explain: Acres can also mean a lot of land. The clue is the word «of»: «acres of forest» means a large area covered in trees. Here the number is not counted exactly. It tells you that the forest is big.
explain: Look at the sentence: «The air so clammy and chill, and not an insect in an acre of it!» An acre is a large space, so saying there is not one insect in it means there are no insects anywhere in that place. Authors often use a measure like this to make a point sound stronger.
explain: Not every country uses acres. The USA, the UK and Canada use them most, while many other places use hectares. If you see an unfamiliar measure in a text, read the words around it, and check a dictionary if the clues are not enough.
fact: An acre is a unit for measuring area, which means the size of land.
fact: «Acres of forest» means a large area of forest, not an exact number of acres.
fact: Acres are used mostly in the USA, the UK and Canada; many other places use hectares.
fact: «Not an insect in an acre of it» means there are no insects at all in that place.
exercise: «A big farm field can be many acres.» What is an acre? | A kind of farm animal | *A unit for measuring the size of land | A type of crop | A tool for digging
exercise: «The air so clammy and chill, and not an insect in an acre of it!» What does this mean? | There are exactly one hundred insects | The insects are very tiny | *There are no insects anywhere in that place | There are lots of insects everywhere
exercise: A farm has 50 acres of wheat. What do the 50 acres tell you? | The number of farmers | The time it takes to grow | The weight of the wheat | *The size of the land
test: A farmer plants wheat on 3 acres. What do the 3 acres tell you? | The price of the seeds | The number of farmers | *The amount of land | The weight of the crop
test: Which phrase means "for every acre"? | not an insect | acres of | snowy mountain passes | *per acre
exam: The rangers look after acres of forest. What does «acres of forest» mean? | *A large area of land covered with trees | A type of bird that lives in the forest | A small number of trees | A river full of fish
